    {
      "id": "claim_6644bd73a0cc460685ec7b13f96b2b44",
      "statement": "The `docs` Python CLI is registered as a project script entry point at `pipeline.cli:main` in `pyproject.toml`, making it available as `uv run pipeline <command>` or (after installation) as `docs <command>`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pipeline/cli.py#L231-L246",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0ed3778ddcb7c00e56acea23b04e7ab2b050d82f808657e2934150c0e320a20b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://pyproject.toml#L55-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:380f3956c325a32028bc599a2de1d6da248085ae5b19b0468503d4df12660bf7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b4df0862630e4f4686d16b149c650c70",
      "statement": "Make targets in the Makefile wrap the Python CLI commands: `make dev` runs `uv run pipeline dev`, and `make build` runs `uv run pipeline build`, enabling convenience invocation via Make.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Makefile#L6-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:12472bfb50bed2773bee4014d9ad5aceca8e31004b3df79ccd2db6a8a77c119d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e62604ae51914795a1343d6d78dfc916",
      "statement": "`docs dev` orchestrates development by: (1) optionally performing an initial full build via `build_command()`, (2) starting a `FileWatcher` monitoring `src/` for changes and triggering incremental rebuilds, and (3) launching the Mintlify dev server (`mint dev --port 3000`) in the `/build` directory with log forwarding, then continuing to watch until interrupted or a process exits abnormally.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pipeline/commands/dev.py#L51-L90",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bfbe7ba05001315219bef3cd38c28b8fed3006b0da00c646e5e6120e690e76d4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://pipeline/commands/dev.py#L92-L150",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1124dfedebaed7a40c7a0f512f8d431968b92350c974ac30cf4052bc30758079:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c9ce6f491a8d42f3aee3546cea5d24a5",
      "statement": "The `--skip-build` option causes `docs dev` to skip the initial build and reuse an existing `/build` directory, useful for resuming development after interruption; it warns if `/build` does not exist.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pipeline/cli.py#L256-L261",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6e54de518e7779083e87d1f806a5beb4c3ee7edc7537f6f1cd19bc2e77f267c7:"
